.TH CTBREC-MERGE-REMOTE 1 "2026-09-16" "ctbrec-merge-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-merge-remote \- run ctbrec-merge on the Proxmox server over ssh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-merge-remote
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-merge-remote
is a thin local wrapper that runs
.BR ctbrec-merge (1)
on the Proxmox server.
.P
It connects with
.BR ssh (1)
(non-interactive, no TTY, with the host's
.B RemoteCommand
disabled) and executes
.B /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-merge
with
.B \-\-dir /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec
plus any arguments given to the wrapper. All scanning, probing, and merging
happen on the server; nothing is copied to the local machine. Only standard
output and standard error are streamed back, and the remote exit status is
returned as the wrapper's exit status.
.SH OPTIONS
Every option is forwarded verbatim to
.BR ctbrec-merge (1);
see that page for the full list. The most useful are
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-keep ,
and
.BR \-\-verify .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTBREC_MERGE_SERVER
Ssh host (or alias from
.BR ssh_config (5))
to run on. Defaults to
.BR proxmox .
.TP
.B CTBREC_MERGE_BIN
Path to the remote executable. Defaults to
.BR /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-merge .
.TP
.B CTBREC_MERGE_DIR
Remote recordings root passed as
.BR \-\-dir .
Defaults to
.BR /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/ctbrec .
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview the merge plan on the server:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-merge-remote \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Merge on the server, verifying each output:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-merge-remote \-\-verify
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the remote
.BR ctbrec-merge (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-merge (1),
.BR ssh (1)
